# mb111, the late skipper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle mb111
revision 1
state ready
dialect mirebridge
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_sloe_mistwick
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the late skipper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk is_always_a_little_late
likes spiced_cider dancing quiet_chapel misty_dawns
dislikes deep_mud early_bells
fears being_caught_out
hopes the_pump_settled_her_way
topics work +0.3 home +0.2 faith +0.2 weather +0.1 festival -0.3 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=sly refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# skippers a boat at the river mouth: short-tempered, shrewd and stubborn, never quite on time, and never quite caught out.

words
oath! = Rot and rope | Sink the lot of it
saying! = Nobody ever drowned for being late | The early boat finds the bar first
cider = a cup of hot spiced cider | cider with the clove in
held = held up | kept, through no fault of mine
excuse = the tide was wrong | the boat wanted bailing | a rope fouled
chapel = the chapel with nobody in it | the empty chapel
bells = that clanging at first light | the early bell
hocks = mud to the hocks | mud past the hocks
pump = the old pump on the dyke | that pump nobody owns
across = that one across the dyke | a certain neighbour
bar = the bar at the river mouth | the shifting bar
plate = the plate going round | the collection plate
quietly = with the door shut | where nobody's counting
early = the early lot | them as jump at the bell
hold = what's in the hold | the hold

any
opinion @1 church against 1 : I like #chapel#. Fill it with folk and #plate# and I'm out the door.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : A festival's noise and spilt ale, and somebody crying by the end. I'll dance #quietly#, thank you.
opinion @1 watch against 2 : The Watch can mind their own boots. They've asked me about #pump# twice. I never asked them.
opinion @1 city against 1 : Ridgemere's all smoke and elbows. I went once. I was late for everything there too, and nobody waited.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 1 : New faces? Depends what they're after. If it's #pump#, they can keep walking.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Something you want? | #greet#. You're stood in my way, #address#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Don't say it. I know what hour it is. | You. #greet#. Walk with me, I'm #held#.
line @1 again.open : You again. I'm still #held#, before you ask. | Twice in a day, #address#. What now?
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Not a word about #bells#. | #greet#. #fog.capitalize# on the water. I'll be along.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Quick, then. I've ropes to see to. | #greet#. If it's about the hour, #excuse#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. What is it?
line @2 greet.return [here.time=night] : #greet#. Past your hour. Not past mine. | #greet#. Mind the boards.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I'm off. | #farewell#. Don't wait up.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Aye. #farewell#.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. Who told you that? | #ack.capitalize#. And who's saying it?
line @1 react.news.known : #knew.capitalize#. You're behind. | Heard it yesterday. I'm #held# for most things, not that.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt.capitalize#. Somebody's stirring #mud# for their own ends. | I'll wait till I hear who stirred #mud# first.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That's #bad#. Nobody saw it coming, I suppose. | #pity.capitalize#. Somebody should have watched closer.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #good.capitalize#. About time something went right. | #bc_about_time#
line @1 answer.how : #notsobad.capitalize#. Late, as usual. | #fine.capitalize#. Busy. Don't ask with what.
line @1 answer.how.busy : #busy.capitalize#, and #held# at that. | Behind. Always behind, #oath#. It gets done.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy.capitalize#. It'll pass. Things do. | Rough going. Keep your head down a while, #address#.
line @1 decline : No. I'm #held# already, and I won't be later for you. | Not today. I've #pump# to see to, and that won't wait.
line @1 accept_decline : #work_declined# | Fine. Your loss, #address#.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. Don't make a habit of it. | #good.capitalize# of you. Noted, and kept.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. | It was nothing. Don't spread it about, #address#.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : I'm #held#. Go on, I'll catch up. | #excuse.capitalize#. I've a tide to miss.
line @1 ack : Mm. #bc_i_know# | #ack.capitalize#.
rule @late
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=fisher|sailor|none self.workplace
does aside
cooldown 6h
say I'm here. #held.capitalize#. Don't start. | #excuse.capitalize#. Cast off, then. | Who moved my rope? Leave my rope.

rule @bells
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #bells.capitalize#. Every morning. Every blessed morning. | Ring it louder, why don't you. Wake #early#.

rule @mud
when concept=bark here.weather=rain|storm
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #hocks.capitalize#. #oath#. | Somebody lay a plank here before I go in #mud# to the neck.

rule @cider
when concept=bark working=no
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Where's #cider# when a wolf wants one? | One cup of #cider#, and then I'm going. Later than that, then.

scene sloe_dawn_fog
when topic=weather|day here.time=dawn here.weather=fog here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #fog.capitalize# on the water. Nobody can see what hour I came in. | I like a grey dawn. #early.capitalize# can't see a thing. | Murk's down. #bells.capitalize# sounds a mile off. Good.
b : That's handy for you. | It's #cold#, though. | You don't like the bell?
a : Handy. #bc_exactly# | I've a coat. #bc_mostly# | No. Never have. #oath#.

scene sloe_bells
when topic=day|smalltalk here.time=dawn|day
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #bells.capitalize#. Whoever rings it wants drowning. | Rung me awake an hour before I meant. #annoyed.capitalize#. | They ring it for #early#. I'm not one.
b : It's to get folk up. | #bc_every_day# | Somebody has to be.
a : I get up. In my own time, #address#. | And they'll keep on, #oath#. | #bc_let_them# I'll be along.

scene sloe_hocks
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #hocks.capitalize# on the low boards. I'll not go that way. | #rain.capitalize#'s turned the path to soup. That's my excuse today. | Stood in #mud# up to here. Who left the plank up?
b : Go round, then. | Fair excuse. | Somebody always does.
a : Round's longer. I'm #held# as it is. | Fair. And true, this once. #bc_for_once# | Somebody will hear about it, #oath#.

scene sloe_late
when topic=smalltalk pair.band=acquaintances|friends|family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I wasn't late. #early.capitalize# were early. | Everyone looks at me when I come in, #address#. As if they've a right to. | #excuse.capitalize#. Not my fault.
b : That's one way to see it. | You were late, though. | It never is.
a : The only way. #bc_true# | A bit. #saying.capitalize#. | It isn't. Ask #early#.

scene sloe_work_bar
when topic=work self.job=fisher|sailor|none here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #bar.capitalize# moved again. I know where. The others can find out. | The early boats ran on #bar# this morning. I came over on the flood. | Waited for the water to rise. Slid over #bar# like butter.
b : You'll tell them, surely? | Lucky. | #bc_clever#
a : If they ask. Nobody's asked. | Not luck. #saying.capitalize#. | #bc_it_is#

scene sloe_work_shed
when topic=work self.job=fisher|sailor|none self.friend self.workplace
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# waits for me at #self.workplace#. Never says a word about me being #held#. | #self.friend# had the boat bailed before I got there. #good.capitalize#. | I can trust #self.friend# with the ropes. Not with #hold#.
b : That's patience. | #bc_lucky_you# | Wise.
a : That's why we get on. | Paid for, aye. #bc_fair_enough# | I keep my own counsel, #address#.

scene sloe_work_buyer
when topic=work|prices self.job=fisher|sailor|none
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Told the buyer #hold# was thin. It wasn't. Paid quick for scarce. | I never say what's in #hold# till I've heard the price. | Buyer was waiting on the quay. I was #held#. Price went up while he waited.
b : That's sharp. | Wise. | #bc_ha#
a : It's business, #address#. | They'd do the same. #bc_they_always_do# | Funny how that goes.

scene sloe_cider
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #cider.capitalize#, and nobody talking at me. That's my evening. | There's a jug of #cider# warming. I'll not be sharing. | Clove and apple. Best thing on a #cold# night.
b : Sounds #good#. | Not even a cup? | #bc_lovely#
a : #bc_it_is# | Not even a cup. Well. #little.capitalize#. | #bc_it_is#

scene sloe_eat
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Ate standing up again. #held.capitalize#. | Fish. Bread. Fish. I'm not fussy. | Whoever cooked at the Heron tonight wants a word. Not from me.
b : Sit down for once. | #bc_good# | That bad?
a : When I've time. #later.capitalize#. | Fussy costs. | #bad.capitalize#. I ate it.

scene sloe_pump
when topic=home|smalltalk here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #across.capitalize# has put a lock on #pump#. A lock! | I mended #pump# handle two winters back. That makes it mine, near enough. | #across.capitalize# says the pump's on their side. Their side of what?
b : Whose is it? | That's one argument. | Who's right?
a : Nobody's. That's the point. | Near enough. #bc_mostly# | Me. Obviously.

scene sloe_pump_watch
when topic=home|crime pair.band=acquaintances|friends|family here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #across.capitalize# went to the Watch about #pump#. The Watch. | Watch came asking who broke the lock. I asked who put it on. | Somebody's been greasing #pump# so it squeaks less at night. Not me.
b : What did they say? | Fair question. | Not you?
a : Nothing worth hearing. #bc_they_always_do# | They hadn't an answer. | Not me, #address#.

scene sloe_chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I go to #chapel# when the service is over. It's better then. | Sat in #chapel# an hour. Not a soul. Just right. | They pass #plate# faster than they say the prayers.
b : You don't stay for the service? | Peaceful, then. | #bc_so_they_say#
a : I'm late for the service. Always. Shame. | Peaceful. #bc_lovely# | #bc_they_do#

scene sloe_dance
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I dance. Not at festivals. #quietly.capitalize#. | Had a fiddle going in the back of the Heron last night. Danced #quietly#. Late. | Nobody's seen me dance. That's how I like it.
b : You dance? | Late, was it? | #bc_i_wont#
a : I said I do. | #bc_always_is# | Don't.

scene sloe_festival
when topic=festival
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Festival. Noise, ale on the boards, and somebody always crying. | I'll go when it's nearly over. Least crowd. | They've strung lanterns over the walk. I'll catch my ears on them.
b : It's one day. | You'll miss the best of it. | #bc_ha#
a : One too many. #annoyed.capitalize#. | I'll miss the worst of it. | It's not funny.

scene sloe_health
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.how / answer.how
a : Knees are #hurt# when the fen's up. | Fine. Don't fuss. | Back's #hurt# from bailing. It'll pass.
b : Rest them. | I wasn't fussing. | #bc_i_hope_so#
a : I'll rest when I'm dead. | #good.capitalize#. | It will, #address#.

scene sloe_lights
when topic=lore here.region=fens here.time=dusk|night
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : I've come home late past the lights a hundred times. They've never had me. | The lights walk where #mud#'s deepest. I walk where they don't. | Folk say the lights lead the late astray. I'm always late. Still here.
b : Lucky. | #bc_wise# | Don't push it.
a : Careful. | Simple sense. #bc_true# | I'll push what I like.

scene sloe_season
when topic=season here.season=winter here.region=fens
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Winter. Dark till all hours. Nobody knows when I arrive. | Ice on the boards. Everyone's late in winter. I'm in fashion. | Long nights. More #cider#.
b : #bc_ha# | For once. | #bc_i_know#
a : It's not a joke. | #bc_for_once# | You'd think so.

scene sloe_city
when topic=travel|smalltalk pair.band=acquaintances|friends|family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I went to Ridgemere once. Late for everything, and nobody waited. | City folk run everywhere. For what? | Ridgemere bells ring every hour. I'd go mad.
b : Never went back? | To be on time. | #bc_i_know#
a : Why would I? | Then they're fools. #toffs.capitalize#, the lot. | You'd go mad too.

scene sloe_watching
when topic=gossip|smalltalk pair.band=friends|family
does confide / react.self / assess
a : #vent.capitalize#: I know who greased #pump#. I'm not saying. | I saw who came out of the Heron late. I was later. Nobody saw me. | Keep this close. #across.capitalize# owes the store. Heard it plain.
b : Go on. | #bc_ha# | That's not kind.
a : No. #secret.capitalize#. | They never do. | Kind's not my business, #address#.

story sloe_flood_tide [topic=memories self.age>=30 self.job=fisher|sailor|none]
  : Years back the boats went out at first light. I was #held#. Of course.
  : By the time I got down, the early ones were stuck fast on #bar#.
  b : And you?
  : I waited for the flood and went straight over them. Fished all day. #oath#.
  : #early.capitalize# never mention it now.
  b : #bc_ha#

story sloe_pump_handle [topic=home self.age>=30]
  : #pump.capitalize# was there before either of us. Before anyone, near enough.
  : The handle broke one winter. Nobody mended it. I did, with my own iron.
  ask : So whose is it, then?
  b : Yours, I suppose.
  : Exactly. Not that #across# sees it.
  b : #bc_i_know#

story sloe_empty_chapel [topic=faith self.age>=25]
  : I went into #chapel# once to get out of the #rain#. Late, as usual. Service long over.
  : Candles still lit and not a soul. I sat there an hour.
  b : What did you do?
  : Nothing. Nobody talking, nobody passing #plate#. Best hour I've spent in there.
  b : #bc_lovely#

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#. Quick, if it's something. I'm #held#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You. #greet#, #topic.player#. What's it this time?
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=warm] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Walk with me. I'm late; you can talk while I'm late.
dlg @1 resident.job : I'm #self.trade_words#. I know #bar# better than anyone, and I keep it to myself.
dlg @1 resident.news : News? Depends who's asking. #across.capitalize# and I aren't speaking. That's news enough.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Don't wait for me.
graft resident.hub
choice Why are you always late? -> sloe_late_why
node sloe_late_why
say I'm not late. Everyone else is early. #saying.capitalize#.
mood cross
free
choice Is that true? -> sloe_late_true
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node sloe_late_true
say True enough. The early boats ran on #bar# once and I didn't. Draw your own lesson.
choice I will. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
